  "comment": "iOS has no native combobox, so every entry binds against semantics an implementation must produce by hand. That is the point: not free does not mean not required. CBX-07 and CBX-08 used to expect `closed-uncommitted` and `committed` \u2014 strings no platform exposes, each packing a state and an effect together. The state now lives in the machine; each effect is its own requirement, with no trigger of its own, because `when:following:` names the transition that performs it.",
